.TH PLAYSKI 1
.SH NAME
playski \- play a SKINI score through sequencer(2)'s synthesizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B playski
.I file.ski
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Playski
plays a SKINI-format score
.RI ( "NoteOn dt voice midinote velocity" / "NoteOff dt voice"
lines, as in STK's own score notation) through
.IR sequencer (2)'s
CSP-style modular synthesizer, to real
.BR /dev/audio ,
and exits when the score finishes.
.PP
It is a thin wrapper \(em a friendlier name than the raw
.B /dis/lib/sequencer.dis
path \(em around
.IR sequencer (2)'s
own standalone player; see there for the actual synthesis graph, and
.IR sh-synth (1)
for note-by-note or multi-score script control instead of a single
whole-file play.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
playski /appl/lib/bachtest.ski
.EE
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/playski.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR sequencer (2),
.IR sh-synth (1)
